  "seats": "Scripted local decision owners and one stock native oracle. No model endpoints. No private model-study seed.",
  "treatment": "Native deliver versus withhold; both preserve the report barrier. Separately vary which decision owner asks for a card or an inbox, and whether it votes or stops.",
  "first_attempts": "One first attempt for each of 12 public tickets. Do not reissue a failure. Keep a separate, clearly identified qualification if the harness needs a repair.",
  "pass": "All 11 normal native grades and both role action sequences in each usable cell equal the predictions. A deliberately unavailable pair is a native error, not a completed zero or a voluntary stop. Every successful owner receipt must match the corresponding world actions. The stock seat has no owner marker.",
  "live_probe": "During hold-east-report, pause the east executable before it submits its report, after its card returns. Before verifier output or result.json exists, observe east at owner_turn/report with [endorse,card] and west at barrier/vote with [endorse,card,report]. Release east. Both owners must end voted; the original verifier must report a success. A marker is a last observation, not a liveness or deadlock claim.",
  "abort": "Release the pause after at most 60 seconds even if no matching snapshot was seen. Do not infer why a peer waited. A fail is still reported and is not overwritten.",
